temprop=3D"text" class=3D"faq-rich-text w-richtext"><p>Boolean-based blind =
injection compares responses to a condition that should be true against one=
 that should be false, for example using <code>$regex</code> to test indivi=
dual characters of a field. Time-based blind injection introduces a delay, =
for example a <code>$where</code> wait loop in MongoDB, and a significantly=
 slower response confirms the condition was true. Note that some NoSQL data=
bases (notably Cassandra) don=E2=80=99t support timing functions at all, wh=
ich rules out time-based blind testing there.</p></div><div class=3D"w-embe=
